  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory corruption when the number of aggregate\n     terms in a query exceeds the maximum number of columns\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-6965.patch: raise an error as soon as the\n       SQLITE_LIMIT_COLUMN limit is exceeded, so the i16 Expr.iAgg index\n       cannot be truncated and indexed out of bounds\n     - CVE-2025-6965\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory corruption in the FTS5 extension when an\n     FTS5 MATCH query is run against a crafted database\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11822_CVE-2026-11824.patch: validate szLeaf in\n       fts5LeafRead() so the chunk-length integer underflow in\n       fts5ChunkIterate() cannot occur; one upstream change covers both CVEs\n     - CVE-2026-11822\n     - CVE-2026-11824",
